Subject: [PATCH] Platform/Sgi: describe the virtio-net MMIO window

The ACPI virtio-net device uses PcdVirtioNetSize for its memory resource.
Without a platform value, the PCD defaults to zero and Linux does not
enumerate the network device, even when it is enabled in the FVP.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jon Mason <jon.mason@arm.com>
---
 Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap2.dsc.inc | 1 +
 Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap3.dsc.inc | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap2.dsc.inc b/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap2.dsc.inc
--- a/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap2.dsc.inc
+++ b/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap2.dsc.inc
@@ -38,2 +38,3 @@
   gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetBaseAddress|0x0C150000
+  gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetSize|0x10000
   gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetInterrupt|460
diff --git a/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap3.dsc.inc b/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap3.dsc.inc
--- a/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap3.dsc.inc
+++ b/Platform/ARM/SgiPkg/SgiMemoryMap3.dsc.inc
@@ -30,2 +30,3 @@
   gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetBaseAddress|0x0C150000
+  gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetSize|0x10000
   gArmSgiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdVirtioNetInterrupt|186
-- 
